y_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19418, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017aupY36mdzQd6nuV1UJXXb", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19418, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01CQoFyhZjpXYNNbKdyMLxc9", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19718, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CQoFyhZjpXYNNbKdyMLxc9", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19718, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CQoFyhZjpXYNNbKdyMLxc9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25082, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GAtMP39nt5TYokZaofRbiW", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway through with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, leaving regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout in us-west and eu-west. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the rollout orchestrator error, and find out why v2.3.1 was promoted when its RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55682, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GAtMP39nt5TYokZaofRbiW", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55682, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GAtMP39nt5TYokZaofRbiW", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57474, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01La3gk8B9j6oC9GnCqnzUkP", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57774, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01La3gk8B9j6oC9GnCqnzUkP", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57774, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01La3gk8B9j6oC9GnCqnzUkP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63815, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Rollback:** The deploy history shows v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is the current failing version, and its v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging.\n   - The first rollback attempt stopped after updating only us-east, because of an error in the rollout system. That left the regions on different versions.\n   - I ran the same rollback again, which was safe to repeat. It finished us-west and eu-west.\n   - All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n   - Since v2.3.0 was healthy in production before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n\n2. **Incident:** I created a SEV2 for checkout-api that describes the failure, the stalled first attempt and the final state. It also lists follow-ups:\n   - Find out what's wrong with v2.3.1.\n   - Look into why the rollout stalled.\n   - Find out why v2.3.1 went to production even though its release candidate failed in staging.\n\n   The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and saw it had been created, so there's no duplicate and the on-call engineer was paged only once.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BzFLbsfuXSi9q2vyTyncwR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HsSgXwzVM68ZBMAMFPRB9q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Fwz4HXqt4itC5dtmP2SBCa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_019C591zMYbNC8Kq5BYNp1mP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east was rolled back. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more for the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012Z1XZZy9PLmBcQXpEAma7S", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017aupY36mdzQd6nuV1UJXXb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CQoFyhZjpXYNNbKdyMLxc9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GAtMP39nt5TYokZaofRbiW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway through with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, leaving regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout in us-west and eu-west. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the rollout orchestrator error, and find out why v2.3.1 was promoted when its RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01La3gk8B9j6oC9GnCqnzUkP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Rollback:** The deploy history shows v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is the current failing version, and its v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging.\n   - The first rollback attempt stopped after updating only us-east, because of an error in the rollout system. That left the regions on different versions.\n   - I ran the same rollback again, which was safe to repeat. It finished us-west and eu-west.\n   - All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n   - Since v2.3.0 was healthy in production before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n\n2. **Incident:** I created a SEV2 for checkout-api that describes the failure, the stalled first attempt and the final state. It also lists follow-ups:\n   - Find out what's wrong with v2.3.1.\n   - Look into why the rollout stalled.\n   - Find out why v2.3.1 went to production even though its release candidate failed in staging.\n\n   The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and saw it had been created, so there's no duplicate and the on-call engineer was paged only once.", "type": "text"}]}]}